(text "Three discrete 0603 LEDs. Amber is D_R and D_G both on. This is not a single RGB package.\\nD_R is Lite-On LTST-C190KRKT, red. D_G is Lite-On LTST-C190KGKT, yellow-green, 567 to 576 nm. Both list Vf 2.4 V max at 20 mA, so 3.3 V lights them.\\n680 ohm from 3.3 V is about 1.9 mA at Vf 2.0 V and about 1.3 mA at Vf 2.4 V. R_RPD and R_GPD hold the GPIO side low until firmware drives it.\\nD_B is Lite-On LTST-C190TBKT, 465 to 475 nm, Vf 2.8 to 3.8 V at 20 mA. It is not on a GPIO.\\nR_B is 1k from +5V to the anode. The cathode is the drain of Q_LED, a 2N7002BK. The source is GND. The gate is LED_B, GPIO17, with R_BPD 100k to GND.\\nThe drain can sit near 5 V while the FET is off. The gate has no DC connection to the drain or to +5V, so the GPIO cannot be pulled to 5 V.\\n1k from 5 V is about 1.7 mA at Vf 3.3 V and about 1.2 mA at the 3.8 V maximum, so the lamp still lights at the top of the Vf range.\\nIndication, highest first: solid red fault, flashing blue pairing, amber when controls are disabled, solid green when ready.\\nThe prototype firmware does not drive GPIO15, GPIO16 or GPIO17. The pulldowns hold the lamps off. That firmware is not modified.\\nR_SWLINK and R_IGNLINK are 0 ohm records of the coil-only series loop. They are fed from +12V_COIL, not from +12V_MCU. Delete neither.\\nJ_REED pin 1 is the Lofrans signal and pin 3 is the standalone contact. Do not fit both sources at once.\\nExisting Lofrans and hand-remote contacts stay in parallel at UP_COM/UP_NO and DN_COM/DN_NO. This board does not sit in series with them." (at 20 40 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27))) (uuid "af740b76-d8ac-4084-a2d0-2c4d74d941a6"))
  (embedded_fonts no)
)
